    "id": "train-5189",
    "question": "4 friends are running a 4 x 100 relay race.  Mary ran first and took twice as long as Susan.  Susan ran second and she took 10 seconds longer than Jen.  Jen ran third and finished in 30 seconds.  Tiffany ran the last leg and finished in 7 seconds less than Mary.  How many seconds did it take the team to finish the race?",
    "gold": "223",
    "answer": "Susan's time was 30 seconds + 10 seconds = <<30+10=40>>40 seconds.\nMary's time was 40 seconds * 2 = <<40*2=80>>80 seconds.\nTiffany's time was 80 seconds - 7 seconds = <<80-7=73>>73 seconds.\nThe total time for the team was 80 seconds + 40 seconds + 30 seconds + 73 seconds = <<80+40+30+73=223>>223 seconds.\n#### 223"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total time it took for the team to finish the race, we need to calculate the time each runner took to complete their leg of the race and then sum these times.\n\n1. **Determine Susan's time:**\n   Jen ran third and finished in 30 seconds. Susan ran second and took 10 seconds longer than Jen.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Susan's time} = 30 + 10 = 40 \\text{ seconds}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine Mary's time:**\n   Mary ran first and took twice as long as Susan.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Mary's time} = 2 \\times 40 = 80 \\text{ seconds}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine Tiffany's time:**\n   Tiffany ran the last leg and finished in 7 seconds less than Mary.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Tiffany's time} = 80 - 7 = 73 \\text{ seconds}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total time for the race:**\n   The total time is the sum of the times taken by each runner.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total time} = 30 + 40 + 80 + 73 = 223 \\text{ seconds}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total time it took the team to finish the race is \\(\\boxed{223}\\).",
